Palestinian militants wounded five Israelis in an attack on Friday before being killed in a shootout with soldiers, leading Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu to order a lockdown in the occupied West Bank days before Israeli elections. Details by Kethevane Gorjestani, FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32b120c6-cee1-11f1-b519-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e918f89d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32b120c6-cee1-11f1-b519-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e918f89d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37eb889c-ced7-11f1-aa9b-e7afb6a10813</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:57:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank closure as attack wounds Israelis before election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-netanyahu-orders-west-bank-closure-as-attack-wounds-israelis-before-election</link><description>
Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad7c33e-cec9-11f1-b15c-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T184642Z-605967326-RC2UPNAG1F4P-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad7c33e-cec9-11f1-b15c-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T184642Z-605967326-RC2UPNAG1F4P-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d96dc9fa-cec8-11f1-9fd1-e58345e5dae5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:41:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>NYT reports plans for fresh strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nyt-reports-plans-for-fresh-strikes-on-iran-after-the-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Reza Sayah, our correspondent in Tehran Iran, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/247ad3fa-cebc-11f1-9f6f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-090607-090912-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/247ad3fa-cebc-11f1-9f6f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-090607-090912-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29842248-cebc-11f1-8576-1b51f8bed30c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:40:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu orders army to prepare for full West Bank closure after attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack</link><description>
The office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ordered the army to prepare for a full closure of the occupied West Bank Friday after Israeli soldiers shot and killed two men who the military said had launched a "terror attack" near the city of Hebron. Emergency services said five people were injured and evacuated to hospitals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b0629b2-ceb8-11f1-a70d-459e24a86637</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:35:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Israel's Ben-Gvir shares AI videos mocking Gazans as 'donkeys' and sending them to Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261022-israel-s-ben-gvir-shares-ai-videos-mocking-gazans-as-donkeys-and-sending-them-to-paris</link><description>
Israel's far-right minister Itamar Ben-Gvir is using AI-generated videos to mock Palestinians and push political messages ahead of the Israeli general election, including videos magically transporting Gazans to Paris or calling them "donkeys" for choosing to stay. One video has sparked an online spat with France. Artificial intelligence is playing a growing role in the campaign, with parties using deepfakes, bots and AI-generated content, raising concerns about disinformation and the technology's influence on voters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e919d896-ce4e-11f1-bdb8-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-icon.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e919d896-ce4e-11f1-bdb8-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-icon.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27c0a7b8-ce50-11f1-99a0-0d0ef307c500</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:38:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ahead of US and Israeli elections, 3-day joint attack on Iran 'would not radically change conflict'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Federico Donelli, Associate Professor of International Relations in the Department of Political and Social Sciences at the University of Trieste in Italy. Can another three days of military strikes achieve what eight months of confrontation have failed to deliver? Donelli challenges the assumption that a short, intensive offensive would necessarily produce a decisive political outcome. He argues, "the real question is whether military pressure is intended to constrain Iran's capacity, or to pressure Iran to sit on the table." And whether they can translate that capacity into a sustainable political outcome without provoking a wider regional crisis. Regardless, Donelli reminds us that "Iran still has leverage over the US."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c66a7ce-ce2d-11f1-9d8f-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-152144-153307-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c66a7ce-ce2d-11f1-9d8f-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-152144-153307-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ff428-ce2d-11f1-8eed-af0e081df335</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:36:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Reports show US and Israel are planning new strikes on Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-reports-show-us-and-israel-plan-new-strikes-on-iran</link><description>
Reports claim that the US and Israel have ramped up military drills and planned new strikes in Iran, potentially targeting energy sites, drone facilities and missile arsenals. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe660f46-ce29-11f1-adff-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d432d452.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe660f46-ce29-11f1-adff-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d432d452.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb5763c4-ce26-11f1-9bb3-7ff061e04dbf</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:34:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Are fresh US-Israeli strikes on Iran in the pipeline?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261022-are-fresh-us-israeli-strikes-on-iran-in-the-pipeline</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 22: The New York Times's sources report plans for fresh strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections. In other news, the French Senate publishes a 30-step proposal for how to "take back control", just days after protests gave way to riots. Also, how software engineers found and patched up bugs in the language that makes up 70 percent of the internet. Finally, the story of a man for whom what happened in Vegas did not stay there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85419180-cded-11f1-b616-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a83d8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85419180-cded-11f1-b616-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a83d8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcff90e8-cdeb-11f1-82ac-a5297acf9f38</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:32:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French President Macron lands in Saudi Arabia on surprise 'solidarity' visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-president-macron-lands-in-saudi-arabia-on-surprise-solidarity-visit</link><description>
⁠French President Emmanuel ​Macron landed in Riyadh on Wednseday, ‌adding an ⁠unscheduled stop to his ‌ongoing tour of the Gulf ⁠region. The president's office said the visit aimed to demonstrate “France's solidarity” ​with Saudi Arabia in ‌the face of attacks launched by the ‌Houthis against its territory. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Douglas Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3707c4-cd67-11f1-aaa1-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T142140Z-1388011539-RC2P7OA2A64V-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3707c4-cd67-11f1-aaa1-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T142140Z-1388011539-RC2P7OA2A64V-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a12ac1b0-cd65-11f1-b94f-15fe03609a5d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:54:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Egypt mulls joining Saudi Arabia in war against Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/egypt-mulls-joining-saudi-arabia-in-war-against-houthis</link><description>
Egypt may be about to join the war against Houthis. Saudi Arabia has come under sustained attack from the Iran-backed group in recent weeks after a collapse of a truce in Yemen in September. Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman visited Egypt mid-September to request potential military support from the country – a demand put before parliament by the Egyptian president on Saturday. Story by Camille Corcoran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58ae6a4c-cd3b-11f1-b708-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-091230-091423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58ae6a4c-cd3b-11f1-b708-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-091230-091423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e9a53b2-cd3b-11f1-875c-2998bf6362e4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:02:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: French president addresses fuel supplies during Gulf tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-french-president-addresses-fuel-supplies-during-gulf-tour</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said on Tuesday he had secured the delivery of an additional 200,000 tonnes of diesel per month from the United Arab Emirates and Bahrain. He is currently in Doha as part of a tour of the Gulf. "We are reducing our dependency" he said whilst speaking to the press on October 21.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/804dd8ee-cd36-11f1-ac0a-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-112430-115100-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/804dd8ee-cd36-11f1-ac0a-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-112430-115100-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8616c830-cd36-11f1-ac62-95f5248e5287</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:18:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Egyptian involvement in Yemen 'may actually weaken Cairo's regional role', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261020-egypt-involvement-in-yemen-may-actually-weaken-egypt-s-regional-role-expert-says</link><description>
Egypt's parliament on Monday delayed a debate on President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi's request to authorise military support for Saudi Arabia until next week, state media reported, after an emergency session ended without a decision a day earlier. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr May Darwich, Associate Professor in International Relations of the Middle East at the University of Birmingham. She explains that "this kind of military operation does not really have any objectives or exit strategy so at the moment this might actually weaken Egypt's regional role".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dabb9c0-cd67-11f1-80db-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0144590d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dabb9c0-cd67-11f1-80db-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0144590d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d78f4b26-cccb-11f1-a2b7-c3baaa33dc98</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:18:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Egyptian involvement in Yemen 'may actually weaken Cairo's regional role', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/egypt-involvement-in-yemen-may-actually-weaken-egypt-s-regional-role-expert-says</link><description>
Egypt's parliament on Monday delayed a debate on President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi's request to authorise military support for Saudi Arabia until next week, state media reported, after an emergency session ended without a decision a day earlier. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr May Darwich, Associate Professor in International Relations of the Middle East at the University of Birmingham. She explains that "this kind of military operation does not really have any objectives or exit strategy so at the moment this might actually weaken Egypt's regional role".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dabb9c0-cd67-11f1-80db-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0144590d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dabb9c0-cd67-11f1-80db-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0144590d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ef003d2-ccc8-11f1-89d8-8d35450d33a9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:57:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Netanyahu is fighting for his political career', expert says a week ahead of crucial vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-is-fighting-for-his-political-career-expert-says-a-week-ahead-of-crucial-vote</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu basked in Donald Trump's endorsement on Monday ahead of close-fought elections, airing a phone call in which the US president predicted he would win and suggested they may again attack Iran together. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Simon Mabon, Professor of International Politics and Middle East Studies at Lancaster University.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/858d62aa-c18a-11f1-8b18-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4VA8T6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/858d62aa-c18a-11f1-8b18-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4VA8T6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67639cc2-ccc0-11f1-ab69-e17d25aa21c1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:03:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's decades-long ties with Gulf states built on 'economic development, oil, defence agreements'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-france-s-decades-long-ties-with-gulf-states-built-on-economic-development-oil-defense-agreements-1</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome François Gouyette, former French ambassador to the UAE and Saudi Arabia. Against a backdrop of violent unrest at home and escalating conflict in the Middle East, French President Emmanuel Macron's Gulf diplomacy underscores the increasingly blurred boundaries between domestic economic security and international strategic commitments. Ambassador Gouyette argues that the visit serves a dual purpose: alleviating France's energy pressures while reaffirming its longstanding defense partnerships with Gulf monarchies. Insisting that "France has to play its role as a key partner," Gouyette portrays French military assistance as an expression of strategic solidarity rather than direct participation in the war with Iran. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d3474bc-cc97-11f1-b7a6-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-140836-141726-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d3474bc-cc97-11f1-b7a6-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-140836-141726-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52e2169e-cc97-11f1-9953-d12189466dc0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:52:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>‘I don't recognise the country I grew up in anymore’: Some Israelis tempted by exile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261020-i-don-t-recognise-the-country-i-grew-up-in-anymore-some-israelis-are-tempted-by-exile</link><description>
From our special correspondent in Tel Aviv – Since 2023, Israel has experienced an unprecedented brain drain. With the October 27 legislative elections approaching, many graduates are considering leaving the country if the right-wing and far-right coalition led by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu remains in power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6993a904-cc6d-11f1-b670-01eaf9681e40</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:07:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg">© David Gormezano, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>David GORMEZANO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Macron secures diesel deals on Gulf visit as fuel prices stoke unrest in France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261020-macron-secures-diesel-deals-on-gulf-visit-as-fuel-prices-stoke-unrest-in-france</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron has obtained commitments to deliver an additional 200,000 tonnes of diesel per month from the United Arab Emirates and Bahrain during a tour of the Gulf, his office said Tuesday as the French government scrambles to address a cost-of-living crisis that has fuelled unrest in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83a39c82-cc68-11f1-ad2c-0f7ccea76ac8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:44:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg">© WAM via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>France 'has to assist' Gulf states, diplomat says as Macron makes three-day visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261019-france-has-to-assist-gulf-states-diplomat-says-as-macron-makes-three-day-visit</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron is making a three-day visit to the Gulf states focused on fuel supplies and strategic ties. The French leader will first visit Kuwait before heading to the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain and Qatar. The Elysée Palace said Macron would seek commitments for additional deliveries of diesel and petrol that could increase supplies available to France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f90ec2-cbb8-11f1-aa50-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a120f6d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f90ec2-cbb8-11f1-aa50-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a120f6d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b189c3c-cb9b-11f1-bda7-1988d4dc9461</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:43:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Inflation squeezes households as Lebanon's economic crisis persists</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261019-inflation-squeezes-households-as-lebanon-s-economic-crisis-persists</link><description>
Lebanon's economic crisis has dragged on since 2019. A re-igniting of Israel's war with Hezbollah derailed the weak recovery seen last year. The World Bank now forecasts that the Lebanese economy will shrink by 6.4 percent this year, with inflation expected to reach around 17.5 percent. A growing divide is visible everywhere: in households, in businesses and even in consumer habits. Our correspondents Serge Berberi and Renée Davis report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a41d5f50-cba7-11f1-9113-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a644ee1b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a41d5f50-cba7-11f1-9113-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a644ee1b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a73357e-c976-11f1-b135-e1f288cffd1d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:18:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Serge BERBERI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>World Food Programme to end aid for half a million in Gaza due to funding shortfall</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261019-world-food-programme-to-end-aid-for-half-a-million-in-gaza-due-to-funding-shortfall</link><description>
The UN World Food Programme has warned that funding shortages will leave about 500,000 people in the Gaza Strip without critical food aid in a territory where two thirds of the population remains acutely food insecure. The WFP said it is reducing its monthly assistance from 1.6 million to 1.1 million people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/967a6c90-cb8d-11f1-bcf9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291491573638.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/967a6c90-cb8d-11f1-bcf9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291491573638.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">264b5dda-cb8d-11f1-a8ea-5dd735243c08</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:33:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/967a6c90-cb8d-11f1-bcf9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291491573638.jpg">©  Abdel Kareem Hana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump endorses embattled Israeli PM Netanyahu ahead of October 27 election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261018-trump-endorses-embattled-israeli-pm-netanyahu-ahead-of-october-27-election</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Sunday endorsed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ahead of Israel's October 27 elections. It was not clear what impact the endorsement would have on voters, since many Israelis have expressed disappointment with Trump over the outcome of the Iran war and the US president's ceasefire proposal.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c3ce8c8-cb0e-11f1-946e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T155301Z-1509213277-RC2KQIA83EQP-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c3ce8c8-cb0e-11f1-946e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T155301Z-1509213277-RC2KQIA83EQP-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">408e0d16-cb0e-11f1-a2cd-d5b28594da17</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:25:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c3ce8c8-cb0e-11f1-946e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T155301Z-1509213277-RC2KQIA83EQP-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-TRUMP.jpg">© Jonathan Ernst, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli settlers attack European delegation convoy in West Bank, beat French mayor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-israeli-settlers-attack-european-delegation-convoy-in-west-bank-beat-french-mayor</link><description>
Israeli settlers on Saturday attacked a convoy carrying a European delegation in the occupied West Bank, beating up a 78-year-old  French mayor. While Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu – who is just days from a crucial election – described the incident as a "smear" campaign against Israeli settlers, France's top diplomat urged Israel to "urgently halt criminal violence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99f3ef8a-ca3a-11f1-b233-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3CR48X.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99f3ef8a-ca3a-11f1-b233-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3CR48X.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac33bc48-ca3a-11f1-b5e9-d9bce0c9d1b7</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:58:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99f3ef8a-ca3a-11f1-b233-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3CR48X.jpg">© Hazem Bader, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis claim responsibility for fresh missile strike on Aden airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-yemen-s-houthis-claim-responsibility-for-fresh-missile-strike-on-aden-airport</link><description>
Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi group claimed responsibility after two missiles struck Aden International Airport on Friday, saying they had targeted a weapons depot as well as a military command headquarters. The Aden Security Department said a Yemenia Airways flight bound for Cairo had been preparing for takeoff when the attack took place.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">51d31896-c9ec-11f1-a58e-a9bb97da8e14</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:00:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg">© Abdulnasser Alseddik, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US journalist injured during Israeli settler attack on West Bank olive harvest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261016-us-journalist-injured-during-israeli-settler-attack-on-west-bank-olive-harvest</link><description>
About 80 Israeli settlers set fire to olive trees and threw stones at Palestinians in a West Bank village Friday, injuring at least two people, including a US photojournalist with The Washington Post. The coordinated attack came as violence by settlers is on the rise during the olive harvest in the occupied Palestinian territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89f613f2-c96c-11f1-b53b-a3afa13a0591</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:01:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg">© Ahmad Gharabli, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia postpones major sporting events amid Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-postpones-major-sporting-events-amid-houthi-attacks</link><description>
Several major sporting events in Saudi Arabia have been cancelled or postponed as a result of repeated deadly attacks from Iran-backed Houthi rebels against the Kingdom's airports and infrastructure. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Guy Barton, Visiting Fellow at Lancaster University and co-creator and co-host of The FootPol Podcast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da51f614-c8d5-11f1-aa87-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-213110-214026-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da51f614-c8d5-11f1-aa87-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-213110-214026-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dfe2d774-c8d5-11f1-84a0-ebd1ed049b0f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:31:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthi attack on palace used by Yemen government in Aden kills five</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthi-attack-on-palace-used-by-yemen-government-in-aden-kills-five</link><description>
At least five people were killed and 16 wounded Thursday in a Houthi missile and drone attack on the palace located in Yemen's interim capital – the southern port city of Aden, used by the country's internationally recognised government, an official said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27f1fba8-c8cc-11f1-b6d1-f56d77e2991f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:57:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg">© Social media via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Election delay 'a terrible disappointment', Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi called the postponement of the first legislative elections in 20 years to September 2027 "a terrible disappointment" for a generation that has never had a chance to vote. He also dismissed the citing of Israeli restrictions as an excuse, pointing instead to a "rejection" of change among ageing Palestinian leaders.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062cef5e-c89b-11f1-9274-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-SAMER-SINIJLAWI-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062cef5e-c89b-11f1-9274-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-SAMER-SINIJLAWI-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa9785f0-c877-11f1-b167-2f6a248273a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:17:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>War escalates between Houthis and Riyadh: How did we get here?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261015-war-escalates-between-houthis-and-riyadh-how-did-we-get-here</link><description>
To discuss the ongoing conflict between the Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed coalition, we speak to Jules Grange Gastinel, a researcher at France's CNRS research body specialising in the Houthi movement. He tells us why the conflict has escalated and what the Houthis want.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dee9186e-c89f-11f1-9be4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a8242456.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dee9186e-c89f-11f1-9be4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a8242456.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ed87506-c87c-11f1-98a8-af119fcfe771</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:16:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis deny targeting holy city of Medina after Saudi Arabia says it intercepted missile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthis-deny-targeting-holy-city-medina-after-saudi-arabia-says-intercepted-missile</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis denied carrying out an attack on Saudi Arabia on Thursday, shortly after Riyadh said it had intercepted a missile targeting the region around the holy city of Medina. Riyadh also accused Tehran of stoking tensions between the Houthis and government forces in the latest escalation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cce943c-c87d-11f1-8d45-fb20c1b501ef</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg">© Majed Al-Charfi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Growing ambitions’: Dr. Kendall on Houthis’ quest to be recognised as Yemen’s ‘legitimate' leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders</link><description>
What is the strategic logic behind the Houthis’ increasingly high-risk confrontation with Saudi Arabia? “Their experience in the past is that threats pay,” explains Dr. Elizabeth Kendall, Middle East specialist and President of Girton College, University of Cambridge. Dr. Kendall argues that the movement’s increasingly audacious military operations are not merely expressions of ideological hostility or Iranian influence, but calculated instruments of political coercion aimed at securing legitimacy, expanding territorial control and strengthening its negotiating leverage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fb60fa-c7ed-11f1-8501-43b1ddbf6a9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:18:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
